# Three substantive Mathlib gaps — partial fillings

This file attempts the three substantive remaining tasks from
[`mass-tower-deeper-fillers.md`](mass-tower-deeper-fillers.md):

(1) **`BlochGroup F` quotient.** Free abelian group on
    `(F \ {0,1}) × (F \ {0,1})` modulo the 5-term pentagon
    relation, plus the antisymmetry `[x] + [1/x] = 0`.
(2) **Pentagon identity for `Cl_2`.** The 5-term identity in
    sine-form, derivable from the standard `Li_2` pentagon via
    imaginary-part extraction.
(3) **Faddeev-Kashaev quasi-classical limit.** Convergence of
    `(1-q) · log Φ_n(x; q) → Li_2(x)` along the joint scaling
    `q → 1, n → ∞, n(1-q) → ∞`.

Each piece is partially formalised: enough Lean structure to
encode the statement and produce a sorry-free conditional theorem,
not enough to close the substantive content unconditionally
(which requires either upstream Mathlib contributions or
~hundreds of additional lines of Lean infrastructure). The class
hooks below are the §3b-cond surrogates downstream blocks already
use.

